WEBVTT

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.040
Tomorrow...

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:24.010
...someone very precious to me.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:31.660
Oh?

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.920
My keychain...

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:34.230
No way...

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:36.860
Did I drop it somewhere?

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.300
Morning!

00:00:44.740 --> 00:00:45.610
Kaori!

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:47.240
Airi-chan...

00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:47.860
Morning.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:49.850
So you're alone today?

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:52.030
Yeah, kind of.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:53.110
Did you have a fight or something?

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:54.600
Not really.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.400
Sou's pretty thick, huh?

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:59.420
If it ever gets really bad,
I'll give him an earful for you.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.750
You know, you two should just
get together already.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:09.290
But we're not like that.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.300
You're not being honest
with yourself either, Kaori.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.250
It's seriously amazing!

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:52.150
Wow.
It's seriously amazing!

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:54.150
It was on TV yesterday, but it's just incred—

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:55.450
What the heck, Kaori?
It was on TV yesterday, but it's just incred—

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:56.900
Let me know if you're leaving without me.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.900
But you were taking too long.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.820
That's nothing new, is it?

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:03.870
What? Another marital spat?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:06.740
Sheesh, we're just childhood friends.

00:03:06.990 --> 00:03:08.990
Yeah, we are, aren't we?

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.250
Hey! Everyone in your seats!

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.210
We're starting homeroom.

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:15.210
Come on, drop the idle chitchat.

00:03:15.210 --> 00:03:16.170
Day monitor!

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:20.080
Next, we have "Chunagon mairi-tamaite."

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:22.270
First of all, "mairi," as in "mairu," is deferential language,

00:03:22.270 --> 00:03:23.450
so "the Chunagon approached,"

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.850
which equals respectfulness toward the Chugu empress consort.

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:28.760
Now, the "tamaite" that comes after.

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:30.160
This is respectful language...

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.370
Yui-chan, what are you doing?

00:03:35.370 --> 00:03:36.820
Oh, Sasaki-san.

00:03:36.820 --> 00:03:39.320
Could it be that you're here to see Sou-kun?

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:42.040
What? No, to see you.

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.130
Me?

00:03:43.130 --> 00:03:46.080
Could I have a little of your time tomorrow after school?

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.080
There is something I want
to talk to you about.

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.760
Sure, but...

00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:53.440
I will come get you
when the closing homeroom ends.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:54.910
Okay, got it.

00:03:54.910 --> 00:03:55.460
Yui.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:57.350
You need something?

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.630
Bye.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:00.730
Oh...

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.800
Kaori's been weird since this morning.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.470
Do you suppose something happened?

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.640
Uh, no idea...

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:24.570
Hey.

00:04:24.570 --> 00:04:27.610
The fried chicken meal today? Fancy.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.450
Plain udon noodles for you again, huh?

00:04:30.530 --> 00:04:31.900
Leave me alone.

00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:32.780
On a diet?

00:04:32.780 --> 00:04:34.330
I <i>like</i> udon noodles.

00:04:34.610 --> 00:04:35.820
Oh, that reminds me.

00:04:35.820 --> 00:04:38.750
Today, at seven o'clock,
we're meeting up at Lighthouse Park.

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.760
Yes, yes, the stars.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.130
So, what about Kaori?

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.080
She's being a little weird today.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:46.320
Do you know anything?

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.060
<i>I</i> should be asking <i>you</i> that.

00:04:48.060 --> 00:04:49.890
I'm sure this is your fault somehow.

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.990
Make sure you really see her, okay?

00:04:54.860 --> 00:04:55.850
Huh?

00:04:59.600 --> 00:05:00.440
Hey!

00:05:02.070 --> 00:05:04.320
Ooh, these turned out great.

00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:07.070
This one is my favorite.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.330
You look good in it as well, Yui-san.

00:05:09.990 --> 00:05:11.830
It is a wonderful photo.

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:14.040
Are there any more places
where we could put these up?

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:17.000
Let me think.

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:19.670
As I recall, there's a bulletin board here...

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:23.340
Want me to get it?

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.750
No, I'm okay.

00:05:33.810 --> 00:05:34.570
This one.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.340
Look at this exquisite angle!

00:05:39.340 --> 00:05:40.820
How radiant the subject looks!

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.070
It's one artistic shot.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.860
Which one?

00:05:47.410 --> 00:05:49.530
What are you doing?!

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.870
I'm going back to the classroom.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:52.560
What?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.500
Oh...

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:04.110
Hey, what's going on?

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:05.460
Beats me.

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.560
Go for it!

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:12.700
Kaori!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:16.850
Take that!

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:21.270
No worries!

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:24.360
No worries, Kaori!

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:28.440
Sasaki-san looks cute no matter what she's doing, doesn't she?

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:35.160
Akiyama, quit gawking at Sasaki-san!

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:37.830
Hm?

00:06:38.740 --> 00:06:39.500
What is it?

00:06:39.950 --> 00:06:41.790
Someone out there take your fancy?

00:06:41.790 --> 00:06:42.380
What?

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:44.250
No...

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:49.850
Hey, did you hear about how a girl
from Class C saw a ghost yesterday?

00:06:49.850 --> 00:06:52.100
What? So it showed up again? Really?

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:54.780
Kaori, let's go to club—

00:06:54.780 --> 00:06:57.100
Sorry, I'm going straight home today.

00:06:57.100 --> 00:06:59.950
What? Did something come up?

00:06:59.950 --> 00:07:01.990
Yeah... Sort of.

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:03.950
Bye.

00:07:03.950 --> 00:07:05.070
Hey...

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:20.250
You should go after her.

00:07:20.520 --> 00:07:22.960
It's about time you fessed up, Sou.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:24.810
What'd you do?

00:07:24.810 --> 00:07:26.890
Steal her underwear? Perv on her?

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:27.920
Did you touch her boobs?!

00:07:27.920 --> 00:07:29.380
I didn't do any of those things!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.470
Then please hurry up and apologize!

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.380
But I just said I didn't do those things...

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:42.200
Sou-san being a pervert is nothing new, but...

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:43.120
What?

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.120
I'll be unhappy if we're not all there tonight.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:49.110
This is an important
Astronomy Club event too, after all.

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.050
Yes, ma'am.

00:07:59.760 --> 00:08:00.500
I'm back.

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:03.000
Welcome home.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:06.480
Hey, Kaori, did I do something?

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:09.810
You won't even make eye contact,
and now you're skipping club too?

00:08:09.810 --> 00:08:11.400
No.

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:15.010
It's my turn to make dinner tonight,
so I wanted to get back early.

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:18.260
Why are you making up these excuses?

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:25.270
Airi-chan...

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.580
<i>Let's see the stars together, okay?</i>

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.730
<i>I'll miss you if you're not there.</i>

00:08:30.140 --> 00:08:32.400
Airi was worried too.

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:36.090
And Nagisa-senpai said that if we're going to see the stars, she wants you there with us.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.070
You know, Sou-kun...

00:08:41.640 --> 00:08:44.210
Sou-kun, do you... um...

00:08:47.440 --> 00:08:48.790
I'm back!

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.290
Oh, Shiori-san's home.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:52.560
So?

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:53.130
What?!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.010
Um, f-for your hamburger steak,

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.410
which do you prefer:
grated daikon or Worcester sauce?

00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:58.930
Huh?

00:08:58.930 --> 00:09:00.810
Mm, smells good!

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:02.380
Welcome home.

00:09:02.380 --> 00:09:03.810
So we're having hamburger steak today?

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:06.640
Wait, are you two going out tonight?

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:08.560
Yes, after we eat.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.310
Well, I'll be waiting outside.

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.230
Okay.

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:18.580
You know, Kaori...

00:09:19.850 --> 00:09:21.900
The closer you are to someone,

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:25.040
the more you have to put things into words
to get your feelings across.

00:09:27.760 --> 00:09:29.070
I'm off.

00:09:35.780 --> 00:09:36.970
Hey.

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:38.430
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:40.700
Hey, you're late, Sou!

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.390
She came after all.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.230
What was it with Kaori?

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:49.110
I don't know. I give up.

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:51.480
You're useless.

00:09:56.230 --> 00:09:58.250
Look, those four there.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:10:00.160
That's called the Square of Pegasus,

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:02.080
and it makes up the body
of the Pegasus constellation.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:04.330
What? I don't see it at all.

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:09.100
Pegasus's legs are at the top
and the head is to the bottom, right?

00:10:09.100 --> 00:10:10.270
Yeah, that's right.

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:11.930
And if you go way down,

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.590
that one that stands out is the
first-magnitude star Fomalhaut.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:19.090
I've heard that there are fewer
first-magnitude stars in the autumn sky.

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:22.050
That's why the autumn sky looks a bit empty.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:25.560
But on the whole,
we've got a pretty clear view today.

00:10:33.570 --> 00:10:37.080
Yesterday's starry sky was just as splendid.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:39.320
That's nothing compared
to what it'll be when it's done!

00:10:40.670 --> 00:10:41.280
Oh!

00:10:42.800 --> 00:10:45.130
Um! A Nobel Prize! Billionaire!

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:47.040
Please don't let Jennifer
get taken by some other guy!

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:49.750
You're not going to wish for anything, Yui?

00:10:50.040 --> 00:10:52.350
What? I...

00:10:55.360 --> 00:10:57.920
What about your wish, Akiyama-san?

00:10:57.920 --> 00:10:59.280
Oh, me?

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:03.580
Hmm, please let me enjoy
every day like I am now.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.930
Or something along those lines, I guess.

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:06.860
That's so like you, Sou-san.

00:11:06.860 --> 00:11:08.660
I'm a simple guy.

00:11:12.940 --> 00:11:15.070
I think I'm a little thirsty.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:17.610
I'd like something warm to drink, too.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.920
Oh, I'm feeling thirsty all of a sudden as well.

00:11:19.920 --> 00:11:21.260
Come with us, Yui.

00:11:21.260 --> 00:11:23.020
What? Oh, okay.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.580
Then I'll come too.

00:11:25.000 --> 00:11:26.700
You two have a proper talk.

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:28.830
Huh? Wh-What the heck? Hey...

00:11:28.830 --> 00:11:30.960
You're okay with tea, right, Kaori-san?

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.000
What? Uh, um, I-I'll come, too...

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:34.220
Don't worry about it.

00:11:34.220 --> 00:11:36.050
Well, we'll be right back.

00:11:36.480 --> 00:11:37.600
Sure...

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.050
Thanks for getting us drinks...

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:44.120
Honestly! Sou-san makes things so hard for the rest of us.

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.560
It's about time Sou paid the sniper.

00:11:46.560 --> 00:11:47.590
That's "piper."

00:11:49.030 --> 00:11:51.070
Airi-san, are <i>you</i> okay
with how this worked out?

00:11:51.070 --> 00:11:51.810
Huh?

00:11:51.810 --> 00:11:54.310
I-I don't really...

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.290
Here.

00:11:56.290 --> 00:11:58.560
When you hit a rough patch,
have something sweet.

00:11:58.560 --> 00:11:59.640
Candy...

00:11:59.640 --> 00:12:01.080
A piece of candy?

00:12:01.850 --> 00:12:02.940
Man...

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:06.790
If only I could just go floating up
and get sucked into the starry sky.

00:12:06.790 --> 00:12:08.330
There you go again with your weird ideas.

00:12:11.920 --> 00:12:12.760
Oh, yeah.

00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:15.250
I've got something nice for you.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:16.750
Here.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:21.210
I just happened to find it when we went shopping for supplies yesterday.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.140
It looked so similar to that other one, so...

00:12:24.450 --> 00:12:26.820
You're right. It looks just like it.

00:12:27.380 --> 00:12:28.500
Thank you.

00:12:29.240 --> 00:12:32.600
I know you loved the old one,
but it's probably time you replaced it.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.080
That one was...

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:37.360
You got it for my birthday back in grade school

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.490
to replace Teddy, who'd been swept away by the river.

00:12:41.480 --> 00:12:43.580
It made me really happy, you know.

00:12:44.050 --> 00:12:46.620
I couldn't afford a proper teddy bear on my allowance, so I got that.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:52.490
Actually, I lost that keychain,
and I've been feeling a bit down about it.

00:12:52.930 --> 00:12:54.870
So this makes me really happy.

00:12:55.180 --> 00:12:57.130
It's nothing expensive, okay?

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.910
It's kinda embarrassing to see you so thrill—

00:12:58.910 --> 00:13:01.080
You're no fair, Sou-kun.

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:01.750
Huh?

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:03.880
No fair...

00:13:03.880 --> 00:13:04.630
About what?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:09.140
I really do love you, after all.

00:13:09.140 --> 00:13:09.850
What?

00:13:13.380 --> 00:13:15.330
I finally figured it out.

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:18.380
I don't want us to be just
childhood friends anymore.

00:13:18.380 --> 00:13:21.230
Not as family or like siblings,

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:24.720
but a different kind of love.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:27.660
Uh, well... That is, I dunno...

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:32.400
Hey, how do you feel about Yui-chan?

00:13:32.400 --> 00:13:34.100
H-How do I feel?

00:13:35.120 --> 00:13:38.070
Well, I do think she's an intriguing girl, but...

00:13:39.300 --> 00:13:41.090
Wh-Why?

00:13:43.910 --> 00:13:44.940
Kaori?

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:48.010
Never mind. Sorry for asking a weird question.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:48.760
Okay...

00:13:50.130 --> 00:13:52.560
I won't rush you for an answer.

00:13:53.940 --> 00:13:54.660
Okay.

00:13:55.360 --> 00:13:58.100
Oh, jeez... This is so embarrassing!

00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.910
I wonder where everyone went.

00:14:17.560 --> 00:14:21.610
Alpheratz and Algenib of Pegasus...

00:14:21.610 --> 00:14:24.630
Fomalhaut of Piscis Austrinus...

00:14:26.480 --> 00:14:27.590
Tomorrow...

00:14:37.230 --> 00:14:39.730
Now, the current temperature is eighteen degrees Celsius.

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:40.030
We should be in for a warm day.

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.030
Mom, have you seen my bag
with a red drawstring?

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:42.730
As for the weather today,

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:43.520
Morning.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:43.850
M-M-Morning. I'm going to go wash my face!
As for the weather today,

00:14:43.850 --> 00:14:44.970
it should be clear during the day,

00:14:44.970 --> 00:14:48.240
with scattered showers toward the late evening and night.

00:14:49.880 --> 00:14:52.660
I smell the scent of spring.

00:14:53.260 --> 00:14:57.860
Now, plug in the value we found here as X and solve for the answer.

00:15:04.310 --> 00:15:06.010
What am I going to do?

00:15:15.060 --> 00:15:18.100
Um, where is Akiyama-san?

00:15:19.270 --> 00:15:22.100
He's probably eating somewhere else.

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.520
I'll bet.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:30.590
I can't face Kaori right now.

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:35.720
Sasaki-san.

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:37.790
Yui-chan.

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:42.680
Um, you remember about
after school today, right?

00:15:42.680 --> 00:15:43.380
Yeah.

00:15:46.790 --> 00:15:51.480
You know, Yui-chan, I told Sou-kun...

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.050
Yes?

00:15:54.260 --> 00:15:55.850
Actually, never mind. It's nothing.

00:15:56.530 --> 00:15:58.010
Well, I'll see you later.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.970
And this rhinoceros beetle was just huge.
Like, it wasn't kidding around.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.090
Akiyama-san.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:11.630
Yui, what's wrong?

00:16:11.630 --> 00:16:15.930
Sasaki-san was behaving strangely at lunch,
so I was concerned.

00:16:16.410 --> 00:16:19.180
And you did not come to the club room either,

00:16:19.180 --> 00:16:21.330
so I was wondering if something had happened.

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:23.060
Uh, well...

00:16:27.570 --> 00:16:29.170
Let's talk elsewhere.

00:16:30.710 --> 00:16:34.390
So I mean, why are you so worried about Kaori?

00:16:34.930 --> 00:16:38.640
Could it be that Sasaki-san already confessed her feelings for you?

00:16:38.640 --> 00:16:39.420
What?

00:16:40.500 --> 00:16:42.640
H-How do you know about that?!

00:16:43.100 --> 00:16:46.600
As I suspected. Then, why are you two...

00:16:48.530 --> 00:16:50.490
I haven't given her my answer yet.

00:16:50.490 --> 00:16:51.400
Why not?!

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.940
For what reason?!

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:03.560
As in the previous case, use this chemical formula.

00:17:03.560 --> 00:17:04.120
Now, then...

00:17:12.160 --> 00:17:14.880
What's wrong, Kaori? You seem down.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.640
All right! Let's go blow off some steam at karaoke!

00:17:18.640 --> 00:17:21.500
Oh, I have a little something going on today.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.910
What's this?

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:25.940
And here I was, looking forward
to belting out some songs with you.

00:17:28.400 --> 00:17:31.790
Maybe I <i>will</i> go out for some fun.

00:17:31.790 --> 00:17:34.540
That's the Kaori I know! Eager to please all!

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.320
Oh, you.

00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.590
And this thing, chewed apart
by a cat and all dried up...

00:17:43.680 --> 00:17:44.710
What's wrong?

00:17:45.940 --> 00:17:47.260
That girl...

00:17:47.260 --> 00:17:49.880
She looks a lot like the ghost I saw.

00:17:56.250 --> 00:17:57.700
What are you doing?

00:17:57.700 --> 00:18:01.050
Akiyama-san, where is Sasaki-san?

00:18:01.050 --> 00:18:04.550
Wh-What? Kaori's not around?

00:18:04.550 --> 00:18:05.950
She's in the club room, right?

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:08.200
Please lend me your cell phone!

00:18:08.200 --> 00:18:09.080
Sure...

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:16.840
That's awesome!
Then I'll totally perfect my maracas.

00:18:16.840 --> 00:18:19.530
And I'll play the tambourine.

00:18:22.150 --> 00:18:23.620
Kaori.

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:25.180
Something wrong?

00:18:25.180 --> 00:18:27.580
Oh no, it's nothing.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:35.850
Kaori-san...

00:18:36.490 --> 00:18:38.680
I hear there's a new crêpe place
in front of the station.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:39.760
What? No way! I wanna go!

00:18:39.760 --> 00:18:40.960
This is wrong, isn't it?

00:18:40.960 --> 00:18:42.390
Let's stop by before karaoke!

00:18:42.390 --> 00:18:43.790
Oh, good idea!

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:44.390
Um...

00:18:46.790 --> 00:18:49.860
Sorry. I can't go today after all.

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:51.980
Kaori?

00:18:55.090 --> 00:18:56.570
Where is Sasaki-san?!

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:00.030
What's wrong? You seem so panicked.

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:01.920
If you're looking for Kaori-san,

00:19:01.920 --> 00:19:06.080
I saw her headed for the school gate
with some friends earlier.

00:19:07.700 --> 00:19:08.820
Yui-san?

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:10.170
H-Hey!

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.170
Is something wrong?

00:19:12.700 --> 00:19:13.710
Sou...

00:19:18.470 --> 00:19:19.260
Yui!

00:19:23.670 --> 00:19:25.260
I wonder if she's in the club room.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:28.550
Excuse me!

00:19:29.450 --> 00:19:31.220
Cargo coming through.

00:19:37.190 --> 00:19:38.920
Pardon the inconvenience.

00:19:41.170 --> 00:19:44.870
So, how did things go with Kaori yesterday?

00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:47.620
Uh, if I had to say... well...

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.240
You've got to properly convey your feelings!

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.940
I'm living with a massive regret right now.

00:19:52.940 --> 00:19:56.520
Before I became separated from her so far away,

00:19:56.520 --> 00:19:58.880
I should have said "I love you" to Jennifer!

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.880
Sorry!

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.800
<i>Ten more minutes...</i>

00:20:09.960 --> 00:20:10.810
Kaori?

00:20:11.730 --> 00:20:13.140
Sou-kun...

00:20:13.850 --> 00:20:17.160
Oh, I'm sorry for not taking your call earlier.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:18.010
What?

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:19.760
Oh, that was Yui...

00:20:19.760 --> 00:20:20.620
Kaori-san.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:24.120
Yui-san was looking for you earlier,

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:27.450
and I ended up telling her that
you'd headed for the school gate.

00:20:27.730 --> 00:20:29.050
I see.

00:20:29.050 --> 00:20:32.440
I'm sorry. Please excuse me
from attending club today.

00:20:32.440 --> 00:20:33.460
You're going home?

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:35.710
Yeah. See you tomorrow.

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:37.710
Oh...

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.710
<i>She's not coming.</i>

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:44.220
<i>Could she be somewhere else?</i>

00:20:51.050 --> 00:20:52.090
<i>How?</i>

00:20:53.700 --> 00:20:54.880
<i>It's her!</i>

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:07.280
Sasaki-san, you can't come this way!

00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:13.460
Ow...

00:21:23.230 --> 00:21:25.470
Sou! It's Kaori-chan!

00:21:53.330 --> 00:21:54.260
Yui...

00:23:25.920 --> 00:23:27.500
My dear old alma mater.

00:23:27.500 --> 00:23:28.620
A possible way to save Kaori...

00:23:28.620 --> 00:23:30.160
I would like your help on this research.

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:30.940
The AI unit?

00:23:30.940 --> 00:23:32.190
It wasn't supposed to be like this...

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:33.670
This is absurd.

00:23:33.670 --> 00:23:34.740
Sou...

00:23:36.160 --> 00:23:39.300
Episode nine: "Gateway to the Past."
